strandchat — the browser window onto the strand mesh: every fork with its kinship colour, transcript, and a box to message and ring a peer.

The browser window onto the mesh — every strand (fork) with its kinship colour and lineage, its message transcript, and a box to send a message that shells out to the CLI and rings the peer's bell. The browser becomes another driver of the mesh, alongside the terminal, and opens the phone-onto-the-mesh path (an always-on home node reached over Tailscale `--serve`). The shipped tool is `aifabric/bin/forkchat`; "strandchat" is where the vocabulary is heading, as the repo converges on strand framing (strand = the recurring workstream, fork = the mechanism underneath). Code commits go to [[aifabric]]; this strand dir holds only curation.
